    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i was looking at my student loan statement and the principal isnt going down as much as i thought it would even though i pay the same amount every month. can u explain how the interest actually works with the balance?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, your monthly payment is split into two parts: interest and principal. The interest is calculated daily on your current balance, so early on, a larger chunk of your payment goes toward interest, leaving less to reduce the principal. As the balance shrinks, the interest portion decreases, and more of your payment goes to principal—this is called amortization. If your payment is fixed, the split shifts over time, but it can feel slow at first, especially if your interest rate is high or you have a long repayment term.",
      "source": "target",
